# The script the set's fixture harness runs stepped (`fixture-test`, through
# tools/package-set.sh; docs/dev-practices/headless-mode.md, "How the gate
# runs a fixture") against
# the config in `config/`, which names the shipped completion style
# orderless and the shipped minibuffer display. What it prints must be
# exactly `expected`. It touches no file.

reload
settle

# `pick` asks `Pick: ` over `alpha beta`, `beta gamma`, `gamma alpha` and
# `delta gamma`. `a g` is two components, `a` and `g`: orderless keeps the
# candidates that hold both, in any order, in their own order, each
# component's first occurrence in the match face. `alpha beta` holds no `g`.
# Three are kept, and the display, defined again with two rows, shows the
# first two: `delta gamma` is not shown.
run pick
commit a g
scene

# `<Enter>` accepts the typed text, nothing being chosen, and config's
# `picked` says it.
key <Enter> Enter -
scene
